# Build context hygiene. Without this the 4.9GB persistent_venv and
# node_modules get uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build, which makes
# an otherwise ~2 minute build take many minutes and can exhaust disk on a
# small droplet.

# Virtualenvs — recreated inside the image, never copied in
.venvs/
backend/.venvs/
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Node — the web image runs its own `npm ci`
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Secrets — supplied at runtime via docker compose env_file, never baked in.
# The ** prefix is load-bearing: a bare `.env` only matches the context ROOT,
# so "repo-task executor/.env" (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN) was being
# copied straight into the image layer — and would ship to anyone the image
# is pushed to.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets/

# Python bytecode / caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Local run artifacts
*.log
logs/
outputs/
# `workspace/` alone only matches at the context root — the 37MB of cloned
# repos under "repo-task executor/workspace/" needs the ** form. The quoted
# variant that used to sit here never matched anything: .dockerignore has no
# quoting, so it looked for a directory literally named `"repo-task`.
**/workspace/
**/.ruff_cache/

# VCS / editor / OS
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.DS_Store

# Docs that don't affect the build
doc/
*.md
!backend/**/*.md
